# Simplifix frontend configuration.
#
# Copy this file to .env (`cp .env.example .env`). EXPO_PUBLIC_* variables are baked into the JS
# bundle at build time — restart `expo start` after changing this file, reloading the app alone
# won't pick it up.

# Base URL of the Simplifix backend API this app talks to.
#
# Left unset (commented out) below, the app already falls back to sensible defaults on its own:
#   - Android Emulator : http://10.0.2.2:8000 (the emulator's alias for the host machine's localhost)
#   - Everything else   : http://localhost:8000  (web browser, iOS Simulator)
#
# Only uncomment and set this explicitly for the two cases that need a real address:
#
# Physical phone via Expo Go — use your dev machine's LAN IP (find it with `ipconfig` on
# Windows / `ifconfig` on macOS/Linux). Phone and computer must be on the same Wi-Fi network:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.23:8000
#
# A deployed backend (e.g. Render) instead of your local one:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://simplifix-backend.onrender.com
